WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.470
This is Sha-co-pay, The Six,
a chief of the Plains Ojibwa,

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.990
painted by Catlin in 1832
on the same journey up the Missouri.

3
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.890
He sits in a richly decorated robe,
posed formally,

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.750
the way a European painter
might pose a nobleman.

5
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.950
Catlin often presented
Native leaders this way.

6
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.170
It honored them.

7
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.250
But it also fit his story
of a noble race about to pass away.

8
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.130
Which European portrait
habits can you spot here?
